  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to women, girls, boys, and their families in conflict-affected in Cabo Delgado</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNICEF projects seek to address key underfunded gaps in the response to conflict-affected populations in Cabo Delgado supporting needs of women, girls, and boys: health, child protection, and education. UNICEF implements Maternal Newborn Child Health (MNCH), Management of Childhood Illnesses (iMCI), nutrition and new-born care, Community health services, mainstreaming of gender and PSEA, implements education in crises responsive activities and respond to key child protection needs across Cabo Delgado. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 95,300 people, including 12,019 women, 11,082 men, 72,200 children, and including 10,200 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
